/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   RAPID FIRE — the questions that separate "has read about it" from "knows it".

   Not trivia. Each one is a mechanism question with a short, sayable answer and
   a follow-up that is where most candidates come apart. Format:

     q      the question, as an interviewer would ask it
     a      the answer you should be able to give in two or three sentences
     edge   the follow-up that separates people, or the trap in the obvious answer
     tags   for filtering; domain drives the deck
     d      1 easy · 2 standard · 3 hard · 4 few people get this

   House rules: no claim about who asks what; no invented numbers; orders of
   magnitude are stated as such.
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

